    "narrative": "The Austin Waves project significant offensive upside today, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (77.96) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.27), our two strongest plays. **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against McCullers Jr., where an 18% boost in SP Skill-adjusted projection and the clean #4 spot in the order set a high floor for counting stats. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** leverages a +14% SP Skill adjustment against Houser, and despite a slight penalty from Houser\u2019s elite catcher frame, the combination of his #1 lineup positioning and favorable dynamic platoon alignment makes him a primary engine for our Roto output today. **Gunnar Henderson** (73.50) also deserves mention; even with a pending lineup, he serves as an elite anchor at MI, capitalizing on a slow delivery from P\u00e9rez, Eu that boosts his SB potential to near-peak levels.\n\nThe most difficult decision on our bench was **Nolan Schanuel** (55.01), who hovered just outside the starting rotation. While he benefits from a respectable 4.71 xERA matchup against Schultz, his #7 spot in the batting order limits his R and RBI potential compared to the high-leverage top-of-the-order slots occupied by **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) and **Andy Pages** (65.43). **Sam Antonacci** earns his start with an elite 0.407 xwOBA, proving that his current form outweighs the more traditional power profiles on the bench. Conversely, we are playing it safe with **Jacob Wilson** (48.51); despite the favorable wind conditions, he is facing a premier arm in Wheeler, and he remains a marginal start strictly due to the quality of the opposing pitcher's stuff.\n\nManagers should monitor the lineup status of **Jacob Wilson** and **Gunnar Henderson**, as their scores are anchored to primary hitting positions that have not yet been officially confirmed. We are also tracking a 44% rain risk surrounding **Josh Jung**, which contributed to his benching in favor of players with more stable situational environments. While **Heliot Ramos** (44.75) draws a tougher matchup against Rodriguez, B, his #1 order slot secures his place in the lineup over bench depth like **Coby Mayo** (40.06), whose current lineup volatility and negative platoon splits keep him below our efficiency floor for today.",
